WEBVTT

00:08:59.929 --> 00:09:01.453
(Laughter)

00:09:01.477 --> 00:09:02.692
Yeah.

00:09:03.573 --> 00:09:06.399
And while there are a whole host of ways

00:09:06.423 --> 00:09:10.434
of remembering stuff
in these competitions,

00:09:10.458 --> 00:09:13.116
everything, all of the techniques
that are being used,

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.476
ultimately come down to a concept

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:18.833
that psychologists refer to
as "elaborative encoding."

00:09:19.317 --> 00:09:21.805
And it's well-illustrated
by a nifty paradox

00:09:21.829 --> 00:09:25.413
known as the Baker/baker paradox,
which goes like this:

00:09:25.437 --> 00:09:28.309
If I tell two people
to remember the same word,

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:29.876
if I say to you,

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:33.503
"Remember that
there is a guy named Baker."